  hreflang=None,\n   830→        type_hint=None,\n   831→        crossorigin=None,\n   832→        link_extension=None,\n   833→    ):\n   834→        \"\"\"Append a link header to the response.\n   835→\n   836→        (See also: RFC 5988, Section 1)\n   837→\n   838→        Note:\n   839→            Calling this method repeatedly will cause each link to be\n   840→            appended to the Link header value, separated by commas.\n   841→\n   842→        Args:\n   843→            target (str): Target IRI for the resource identified by the\n   844→                link. Will be converted to a URI, if necessary, per\n   845→                RFC 3987, Section 3.1.\n   846→            rel (str): Relation type of the link, such as \"next\" or\n   847→                \"bookmark\".\n   848→\n   849→                (See also:\n   850→                http://www.iana.org/assignments/link-relations/link-relations.xhtml)\n   851→\n   852→        Keyword Args:\n   853→            title (str): Human-readable label for the destination of\n   854→                the link (default ``None``). If the title includes non-ASCII\n   855→                characters, you will need to use `title_star` instead, or\n   856→                provide both a US-ASCII version using `title` and a\n   857→                Unicode version using `title_star`.\n   858→            title_star (tuple of str): Localized title describing the\n   859→                destination of the link (default ``None``). The value must be a\n   860→                two-member tuple in the form of (*language-tag*, *text*),\n   861→                where *language-tag* is a standard language identifier as\n   862→                defined in RFC 5646, Section 2.1, and *text* is a Unicode\n   863→                string.\n   864→\n   865→                Note:\n   866→                    *language-tag* may be an empty string, in which case the\n   867→                    client will assume the language from the general context\n   